abstract: >-
  Aletheia is an open-source Python/Dash pipeline for quality-control
  filtering of untargeted LC–MS metabolomics and lipidomics datasets. It
  performs per-feature linearity assessment against QC dilution series,
  a two-tier replicate-injection diagnostic, %CV/ICC repeatability filtering,
  and emits curated feature tables together with a fully auditable per-feature
  decision log. Accepts CSV exports from Bruker MetaboScape, MZmine 3, XCMS
  and MS-DIAL, plus a generic CSV loader with manual sample mapping.
